{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show 4809516:docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md | nl -ba | sed -n '1,252p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Phase 2 plan: Axylo 1.0 in TypeScript\n     2\t\n     3\tRevision 3, 2026-11-18. Revised after three independent reviews ([ledger](../reviews/2026-11-18/ledger.md)) and the owner's decisions of the same day (scatter and a compact variant are in 1.0; the mark renderer is decided in M1).\n     4\t\n     5\tThis plan builds the product defined in [02-product-spec.md](02-product-spec.md). Criterion IDs (F1, L1, A2, DX4, P1 …) refer to that spec; finding IDs (R5, D2 …) refer to [01-landscape.md](01-landscape.md).\n     6\t\n     7\t**The release is done when every row of the acceptance matrix passes.** The matrix lives in the repository as data: one row per spec criterion and chart type, naming the test that covers it, with a result of pass, fail or not applicable (with the reason). The Phase 1 comparison is rerun with Axylo included and published, but it is comparison evidence, not the gate: several of its columns are descriptive, and it cannot run the performance budgets.\n     8\t\n     9\t## 1. Public API\n    10\t\n    11\tThe declarations are in [packages/axylo/src/public.ts](../packages/axylo/src/public.ts), and every example below is in [docs/api/examples.ts](api/examples.ts), type-checked against the package by `npm run typecheck`: the examples compile, and the deliberate mistakes fail to compile. (The first revision of this plan carried a separate declaration sketch, `docs/api/axylo.d.ts`; the package replaced it.)\n    12\t\n    13\t### 1.1 Shape\n    14\t\n    15\tOne function per chart type, each taking a target element and a plain options object, each returning the same small handle.\n    16\t\n    17\t```ts\n    18\timport { line } from 'axylo';\n    19\t\n    20\tconst chart = line('#sessions', {\n    21\t  title: 'Daily sessions by channel',\n    22\t  data: rows,              // [{ day: '2026-01-01', channel: 'Direct', sessions: 31713 }, …]\n    23\t  x: 'day',\n    24\t  y: 'sessions',\n    25\t  series: 'channel',\n    26\t});\n    27\t```\n    28\t\n    29\tThat is the whole first chart. Axes, legend, tooltip, keyboard access, description, data table, light and dark colors and resizing are on without further options.\n    30\t\n    31\t| Decision | Reason |\n    32\t|---|---|\n    33\t| Field names over a table | Finding D2: the ten libraries take five incompatible shapes, and the harness had to reshape its fixture a different way for each. Application data arrives as rows. |\n    34\t| One function per chart type (`line`, `area`, `bar`, `donut`, `scatter`) | Each has its own options type, so options that do not apply are type errors (DX3), and bundlers can drop unused chart types. Whether shared code actually tree-shakes is measured on real consumer builds in M7. |\n    35\t| Plain options object, not a builder or a JSX tree | The same object works in the React adapter. Recharts needed eight components for the trend task; the information content was four fields. |\n    36\t| No required configuration beyond data and fields | Findings R11, R15, D1: tooltips, legends, time adapters, margins, colors and accessibility were opt-in somewhere in every library. |\n    37\t\n    38\t### 1.2 Data: one logical table, three forms\n    39\t\n    40\t```ts\n    41\t// long rows: one row per (x, series)\n    42\tline(el, { data: rows, x: 'day', y: 'sessions', series: 'channel' });\n    43\t\n    44\t// wide rows: one column per series\n    45\tline(el, { data: wide, x: 'day', y: ['direct', 'organic', { field: 'referral', label: 'Referral' }] });\n    46\t\n    47\t// typed columns for large data; the row type is inferred from the columns\n    48\tline(el, { data: { columns: { t: new Float64Array(n), v: new Float32Array(n) } }, x: { field: 't', type: 'time' }, y: 'v' });\n    49\t```\n    50\t\n    51\tLong and wide are mutually exclusive in the types: `series` cannot be combined with an array of `y`.\n    52\t\n    53\tRules the three forms share:\n    54\t\n    55\t| Rule | Detail |\n    56\t|---|---|\n    57\t| Ownership | Row arrays are read once and never mutated. Typed columns are borrowed, not copied; the caller must not change them in place, and replaces them through `update`. |\n    58\t| Column lengths | All columns must have the same length; otherwise AX100. |\n    59\t| Missing values | Rows: `null`, or an absent key. Typed columns: `NaN` means missing and does not raise AX103. |\n    60\t| Order | Line, area and scatter are sorted by x internally (F11). `append` expects rows at or after the last x. |\n    61\t| Provenance | Every normalized sample keeps the index of the row it came from, so diagnostics, the table and events point at the caller's own data. |\n    62\t\n    63\t### 1.3 Fields\n    64\t\n    65\tA field is a key of the row, or an object when it needs more. The key is checked against the row type by role: a value axis accepts number fields; text fields are accepted there only with `parse: 'number'`.\n    66\t\n    67\t```ts\n    68\tline(el, {\n    69\t  data: samples,\n    70\t  x: { field: 'ts', type: 'time', timeZone: 'UTC' },\n    71\t  y: { field: 'sessions', label: 'Sessions', unit: 'sessions', tickFormat: { notation: 'compact' } },\n    72\t});\n    73\t\n    74\t// counts that a database driver returns as strings\n    75\tbar(el, { data: pgRows, x: 'day', y: { field: 'count', parse: 'number', missing: 'zero' } });\n    76\t```\n    77\t\n    78\t| Option | Meaning |\n    79\t|---|---|\n    80\t| `field` | Key of the row. |\n    81\t| `label`, `unit` | Axis title; name and unit in tooltip, table and announcements. |\n    82\t| `type` (x) | `'date'`, `'time'`, `'number'`, `'category'`. Inferred when omitted, except that a number is never inferred to be an instant (F4). |\n    83\t| `timeZone` (x) | For instants: `'local'` (default), `'UTC'`, or an IANA zone. |\n    84\t| `format`, `tickFormat` | Readouts and ticks are formatted separately (F6). |\n    85\t| `scale` (value) | `'percent'` (0–100) or `'ratio'` (0–1). Declared, never inferred (F7). |\n    86\t| `missing` (value) | `'gap'` (default) or `'zero'` (F2). |\n    87\t| `parse` (value) | `'number'`, for a text field holding numbers (AX104, AX106). |\n    88\t| `domain` | Author bounds. Widened to zero on bar and area (F1). |\n    89\t\n    90\t### 1.4 Common options\n    91\t\n    92\tSummarized; the declarations are the reference.\n    93\t\n    94\t| Option | Purpose |\n    95\t|---|---|\n    96\t| `title`, `labelledBy`, `subtitle`, `description` | The chart's visible heading and accessible name (A1). `title` may carry a heading `level` and `visible: false`; `labelledBy` points at a heading the page already has. |\n    97\t| `state` | `'ready'`, `'loading'`, `{ error }`, `{ empty }` (L7). |\n    98\t| `legend`, `tooltip`, `table` | On by default; each can be turned off. |\n    99\t| `zoom`, `reference` | Cartesian charts only. |\n   100\t| `compact` | Line, area and bar: marks only, as a static image with a text alternative (spec 3.7). |\n   101\t| `colors` | A fixed color per series name (DX6). |\n   102\t| `messages`, `locale` | Built-in text and formatting locale (A10, F6). |\n   103\t| `strict`, `onDiagnostic` | Diagnostics delivery (section 3.5 of the spec). |\n   104\t\n   105\tThere is no `width`, `height`, `responsive`, `theme`, `palette` or `animation` option. Size comes from the container, colors from CSS, motion from the spec (I5). An unknown key raises AX150 with the closest known name.\n   106\t\n   107\t### 1.5 Handle and commit contract\n   108\t\n   109\t```ts\n   110\tchart.update({ title: 'Sessions' });                 // options\n   111\tchart.append([{ day: '2026-05-01', channel: 'Direct', sessions: 41210 }], { keep: 120 });   // rows\n   112\tchart.zoom(['2026-03-01', '2026-03-31']);            // view\n   113\tconst off = chart.on('hover', point => { … });\n   114\tchart.diagnostics;                                   // current, as soon as any call returns\n   115\tchart.destroy();\n   116\t```\n   117\t\n   118\tFinding D3: the ten libraries have seven update idioms. Axylo has three methods, one per kind of change, with one contract.\n   119\t\n   120\t| Rule | Detail |\n   121\t|---|---|\n   122\t| Order | Calls are applied in the order made. `update({ data })` followed by `append` appends to the new data. |\n   123\t| Two phases | Each call validates and normalizes synchronously: diagnostics are current when it returns, and a `strict` chart throws from that call. Drawing is deferred to the next animation frame, and calls made before that frame are drawn once. |\n   124\t| Atomic switch | Marks, labels, hit testing and the accessibility layer move to a new data revision together. No frame mixes two revisions. |\n   125\t| Patches | A key present in an `update` replaces the old value whole; a key set to `undefined` returns to its default; absent keys stay. No deep merging. |\n   126\t| Rejected changes | A call that throws under `strict` leaves the chart on its last valid state. |\n   127\t| Streaming | `keep` is the number of distinct x values retained. Rows before the last x are accepted through the slower full update and raise AX151. While zoomed to the latest edge the view follows new data; zoomed elsewhere, it stays put. Paused charts buffer (I6). Keyboard focus stays on its datum until that datum leaves the window (A7). |\n   128\t| Teardown | `destroy()` cancels the pending frame, disconnects observers and listeners, and makes later calls no-ops. |\n   129\t\n   130\t### 1.6 Diagnostics\n   131\t\n   132\tThe registry, with each code's level and outcome, is in the spec (section 3.5). Example for the Phase 1 combined dirty fixture (`[10, 20, null, NaN, '40', undefined, 70]`):\n   133\t\n   134\t```\n   135\t[axylo AX103] \"Dirty input\": y field \"value\" has 1 value that is not a finite number (NaN at row 3). Shown as a gap.\n   136\t  Check the calculation that produced it, or send null for \"no data\".\n   137\t[axylo AX106] \"Dirty input\": y field \"value\" mixes numbers with 1 string (\"40\" at row 4). The string is not plotted.\n   138\t  Convert it to a number where the data is produced.\n   139\t[axylo AX102] \"Dirty input\": y field \"value\" is absent in 1 row (row 5). Shown as a gap.\n   140\t  Send null if the value is known to be missing.\n   141\t```\n   142\t\n   143\tThe reader of that chart sees \"Values not shown: 3. See table.\" (F12).\n   144\t\n   145\t`validate(type, options)` runs the same normalization without a DOM and returns the diagnostics, so a server, a test or a coding agent can check a chart before rendering it.\n   146\t\n   147\tDevelopment and production flavours are selected through package `exports` conditions. The script-tag distribution ships `axylo.js` (development) and `axylo.min.js` (production). Errors and warnings print once per code per page in both; hints only in development.\n   148\t\n   149\t### 1.7 React adapter\n   150\t\n   151\t```tsx\n   152\timport { Line } from '@axylo/react';\n   153\t\n   154\t<Line data={rows} x=\"day\" y=\"sessions\" series=\"channel\" title=\"Daily sessions by channel\" />\n   155\t```\n   156\t\n   157\t| Behavior | Detail |\n   158\t|---|---|\n   159\t| Lifecycle | Create on mount, `destroy` on unmount; correct under StrictMode's setup, cleanup, setup. The file is marked `'use client'`. |\n   160\t| Props to options | Field specs are compared structurally, so an inline `x={{ field: 'ts' }}` does not renormalize on every render. `data` is compared by identity; in development, the same content arriving three times with a new identity raises a hint to memoize it. |\n   161\t| Removed props | A prop that disappears is sent as `undefined`, which restores the default. |\n   162\t| Handlers | Replaced without recreating the chart. |\n   163\t| Streaming | A ref exposes the handle, so `append`, `zoom` and `diagnostics` are reachable. When `data` is controlled, a new `data` prop replaces whatever was appended. |\n   164\t\n   165\tThe adapter is prototyped in M3, before the API freezes, because it is the cheapest way to find out whether the core contract survives a second consumer. It ships in 1.0 because finding 1.1 of the landscape shows where everyday charts are written; that is evidence of where charts are written, not of demand for Axylo.\n   166\t\n   167\t## 2. Architecture\n   168\t\n   169\t### 2.1 Pipeline\n   170\t\n   171\t```\n   172\toptions ─► normalize ─► frame ──┬─► view model ─► layout ─► scene ─► mark renderer\n   173\t            │ validate   (authoritative) │   scales, visible range         text renderer (DOM)\n   174\t            ▼ diagnostics                ├─► lookup: exact values by x, by point, by ordinal\n   175\t                                         ├─► summary and table\n   176\t                                         └─► focus model\n   177\t```\n   178\t\n   179\tThe **frame** is the normalized, lossless data: typed columns, a validity bitmap, dictionary-encoded categories, source-row indexes and a revision number. It is the only source for exact values. The table, the summary, keyboard navigation, tooltips and events read the frame. The **scene** is geometry for drawing and may be simplified (F5); nothing reads values back from it. The first draft derived accessibility from the scene, and two reviewers showed that a simplified drawing cannot return the samples it dropped.\n   180\t\n   181\t| Stage | Output | Notes |\n   182\t|---|---|---|\n   183\t| normalize | Frame, diagnostics | The only place raw input is read. Never coerces silently. |\n   184\t| view model | Scales, visible index ranges, series visibility | Domain rules implement F1 and F7. |\n   185\t| lookup | Nearest-x by binary search; nearest-point by a grid index (scatter) | Works on the frame within the visible range; cost bounded independently of the drawing. |\n   186\t| layout | Plot rectangle, tick sets, label boxes, legend and control placement | Implements L1, L3, L8. Takes a text-measurement interface as input. |\n   187\t| scene | Flat list of primitives (`path`, `rect`, `arc`, `rule`, `text`) | Plain data; testable in Node with injected text metrics. |\n   188\t| renderers | Marks; DOM text; accessibility DOM | See 2.3. |\n   189\t\n   190\t### 2.2 Invalidation\n   191\t\n   192\tStages are cached, and the cache keys are explicit. Caching on object identity alone, as the first draft said, would miss font loads, pixel-ratio changes and in-place mutation.\n   193\t\n   194\t| Stage | Reruns when |\n   195\t|---|---|\n   196\t| normalize | Data revision or field encoding changes. `append` extends the frame without renormalizing earlier rows. |\n   197\t| view model | Frame revision, zoom, series visibility, author domains. |\n   198\t| layout | View model; container size; resolved font and text spacing; `document.fonts` finishing a load; locale; any label text. A data-only update reruns layout when the tick labels would change, and skips it otherwise. |\n   199\t| scene | Layout or view model. |\n   200\t| mark raster | Scene; device pixel ratio; resolved colors (L4's triggers). |\n   201\t\n   202\tText is measured with the page's computed font, letter spacing and word spacing applied to the measuring context, and layout reruns when fonts finish loading. The measurement interface is a parameter, so Node tests inject fixed metrics and browser tests use the real one.\n   203\t\n   204\t### 2.3 Rendering\n   205\t\n   206\t**Working assumption: Canvas 2D for marks, HTML for all text.** Text stays in the DOM so that it inherits the page font and color, honors user text spacing and zoom (A6), adapts in forced-colors mode, and can be selected and translated.\n   207\t\n   208\t**This is reopened and decided in M1 by measurement.** The first draft justified canvas by Phase 1's slow SVG libraries, but those create a node per point; the one-path-per-series SVG chart in the harness was fast. With drawing simplified to a few vertices per pixel column (F5), an SVG path per series is small. SVG follows CSS variables and class-toggled themes with no repaint code, adapts to forced colors, prints sharply, needs no pixel-ratio handling and allocates no backing store (a 1,920×1,080 canvas at pixel ratio 2 is about 33 MB). Canvas is likely cheaper for per-frame redraw when streaming and hovering.\n   209\t\n   210\tM1 builds both mark renderers behind the same scene and compares them on: P1, P2, P3, P5, bytes, memory, a runtime theme toggle, forced colors, print, and browser zoom. The scene is renderer-neutral either way, so the choice is contained.\n   211\t\n   212\t**Simplified drawing.** Per device-pixel column and per contiguous run of valid samples, the stroke covers the run's minimum and maximum (F5). One rule for when it applies: more than four visible samples per device-pixel column on average. The pass over visible samples is O(visible) on typed columns and is measured separately from drawing; the vertex count is bounded by width times the number of runs, not by width alone.\n   213\t\n   214\t**No animation system.** First render is not animated (I5). Updates cut, or tween for at most 200 ms where the cost is negligible, and not at all under reduced motion.\n   215\t\n   216\t### 2.4 Document structure\n   217\t\n   218\t```html\n   219\t<figure class=\"axylo\" id=\"ax7\" role=\"group\" aria-labelledby=\"ax7-t\" aria-describedby=\"ax7-s\">\n   220\t  <figcaption>\n   221\t    <h3 id=\"ax7-t\">Daily sessions by channel</h3>        <!-- level from options; or omitted when labelledBy is used -->\n   222\t    <p id=\"ax7-s\" class=\"axylo-summary\">Line chart, 3 series, …</p>\n   223\t  </figcaption>\n   224\t  <div class=\"axylo-plot\" tabindex=\"0\"> … marks … <div class=\"axylo-text\" aria-hidden=\"true\">tick labels</div></div>\n   225\t  <div class=\"axylo-toolbar\" role=\"toolbar\" aria-label=\"Chart controls\">   <!-- one tab stop, roving focus -->\n   226\t    legend toggles · zoom in · zoom out · reset · pause · view as table\n   227\t  </div>\n   228\t  <p class=\"axylo-note\" role=\"status\">Values not shown: 2. See table.</p>\n   229\t  <div class=\"axylo-live\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div>\n   230\t  <div class=\"axylo-tooltip\" hidden></div>\n   231\t  <div class=\"axylo-table\" hidden><!-- built when opened: caption, headers, pager --></div>\n   232\t</figure>\n   233\t```\n   234\t\n   235\tIds are generated per chart. The plot's role, and how a focused point is conveyed, are not fixed here: M1 runs a spike with three candidate patterns and M4 confirms the choice (section 4).\n   236\t\n   237\tDefault styles are applied without injecting a `<style>` element, and a standalone stylesheet ships for pages that prefer to load it themselves. Which mechanism passes a strict Content Security Policy is settled by the M7 test with real headers, not assumed.\n   238\t\n   239\t### 2.5 Repository\n   240\t\n   241\t```\n   242\tpackages/axylo/        core library (src/, test/)\n   243\tpackages/react/        @axylo/react\n   244\tapps/docs/             documentation site; runnable examples are test fixtures\n   245\tbench/                 benchmark harness (04-plan-performance.md), built in M0\n   246\tacceptance/            the acceptance matrix and the fixtures it uses\n   247\tresearch/              Phase 1 evidence and the ten-library harness\n   248\tdocs/api/              the type-checked API sketch, replaced by generated declarations in M0\n   249\t```\n   250\t\n   251\tTooling: TypeScript strict; ESM output with `.d.ts`, plus IIFE files for `<script>` use; Vitest; fast-check for property tests; Playwright on Chromium, Firefox and WebKit; axe-core; size-limit on the packed distribution; API Extractor so that public API changes fail CI until reviewed; Changesets.\n   252\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'for p in core1.review.md core2.review.md core1.fix.report.md core2.fix.report.md; do git show 4809516:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/$p | nl -ba; done'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'for p in core1.review.md core2.review.md core1.fix.report.md core2.fix.report.md; do git show 4809516:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/$p | nl -ba; done'","aggregated_output":"     1\t**Five findings block release.** A strict rejection can alter later data, an encoding update can resurrect evicted rows, and two paths let the reader interact with data that differs from the displayed chart.\n     2\t\n     3\t**Ran** means I reproduced the result in Node. For controller experiments I used the repository’s controller, data, view, layout, scene, lookup, and reader code, with a manual animation-frame queue and recording substitutes for the browser outputs. **Reasoned** identifies conclusions from source inspection. I did not launch a browser.\n     4\t\n     5\t### Blocking\n     6\t\n     7\t1. **B · A rejected strict append mutates the accepted store. Ran.** I created eight series under `strict`, then appended a ninth. The call threw `AX130` and the displayed frame still had eight series. A subsequent valid append to an existing series also threw `AX130`. After disabling strict mode, the rejected ninth series appeared. `store.append()` commits before `finish()` validates the new view. Plan 1.5 requires rejection to preserve the store as well as the visible frame. Prepare the append and its view in a transaction, then commit both after validation. The existing strict-append test exercises an early `NaN` rejection only. [chart.ts:350](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:350) · [lifecycle.browser.test.ts:229](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/lifecycle.browser.test.ts:229)\n     8\t\n     9\t2. **B · Re-encoding an aligned chart loses appended data and restores evicted data. Ran.** Starting at x values `[1,2,3]`, I appended `4` with `keep:2`. The chart showed `[3,4]`. Changing `y` to another valid field restored `[1,2,3]`. A chart created empty, populated by append, then re-encoded became empty again. Explicitly updating `data` with the original array after an append also failed to replace the stream. The controller keeps the initial `options.data` alongside the live store and detects replacement by identity. Plan 1.5 requires call order to determine the data. Re-encode from the retained logical table, honor an explicit data replacement after streaming, and advance the frame epoch on encoding changes as the frame contract requires. [chart.ts:308](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:308) · [contracts.ts:129](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts:129)\n    10\t\n    11\t3. **B · Eviction changes hover events before the new frame is drawn. Ran.** With `[0,1,2]` displayed, I appended `3` with `keep:1` and moved the simulated pointer over `0` before running the frame. The event contained `x:0, y:0, index:0, row:null` for a real input row. The old lookup still supplies the displayed values, but its row source reads the already-trimmed store. Plan 1.5 and DX5 require all parts of that event to come from the displayed revision. Retain evicted source rows until the last displayed frame that can address them is retired. [chart.ts:794](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:794) · [store-rows.ts:107](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-rows.ts:107)\n    12\t\n    13\t4. **B · A deferred failure leaves an active old lookup and can permanently clear axis text. Ran.** I forced the reader stage to fail after a successful draw. The controller emitted the internal-error figure and cleared the text. Moving the pointer then produced the old tooltip. After removing the failure and issuing a title update, the controller resumed drawing with zero axis labels because the cached layout still compared equal. `failSafe()` retains the old ready display, lookup, and layout after clearing their outputs. Publish a complete error-state revision with interaction disabled, invalidate the cleared outputs, and settle readiness against that revision. The browser failure test ends before either hover or recovery. [chart.ts:699](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:699) · [chart.ts:663](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:663) · [data.browser.test.ts:121](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/data.browser.test.ts:121)\n    14\t\n    15\t5. **B · The full figure has no keyboard, legend, streaming, or table controls. Reasoned from the DOM construction. Ran the zoom subscription.** The figure mounts its caption, plot, note, live region, and tooltip. Nothing mounts a focusable plot, toolbar, legend toggles, Pause/Resume, or the reader’s table. A note can say “See table” with no way to open one, and L8’s small-chart fallback lacks its table control. The controller accepts `select` and `zoom` listeners but only emits `hover`. My programmatic zoom produced zero zoom events. Wire the full-chart controls, visibility state, table model, and events to the displayed revision as specified in plan 1.4, 1.5 and 2.4. Preserve the compact chart’s static behavior. [figure.ts:105](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:105) · [chart.ts:183](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:183) · [chart.ts:797](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:797)\n    16\t\n    17\t### Major\n    18\t\n    19\t6. **M · Callbacks can repeat delivery or continue work after destruction. Ran.** An `onDiagnostic` handler that updated only `description` received the same diagnostic twice. A handler that destroyed the chart on its first diagnostic still received the next one. Likewise, a second hover listener ran after the first destroyed the chart. Destroying from a formatter during a frame allowed that frame to draw and repopulate `drawn`. Commit the delivery snapshot before invoking author code, and check the lifecycle generation after callbacks and before publishing frame work. DX5 teardown must take effect inside callbacks too. [chart.ts:285](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:285) · [chart.ts:677](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:677) · [chart.ts:800](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:800)\n    20\t\n    21\t7. **M · Scatter and donut append change the meaning of existing data. Ran.** On scatter with x values `[10,20]`, appending `5` with `keep:2` retained `[5,20]` and produced no `AX151`. Plan 1.5 requires the out-of-order diagnostic and the latest two distinct x positions, `[10,20]`. On both scatter and donut, appending one clean row to typed columns changed an existing silent `NaN` into `AX103`. `appendRows()` materializes every old column row and trims by raw arrival order, also renumbering retained rows. Preserve column missingness and source indexes, normalize ordering keys before eviction, and validate the incoming batch before trimming. For donut, I treated the label as its retention key, as the implementation does. [chart.ts:354](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:354) · [chart.ts:1006](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:1006)\n    22\t\n    23\t8. **M · The empty-state test disagrees with the visible geometry and suppresses omission notes. Ran.** A line joining `(0,0)` and `(10,10)`, zoomed to `[2,4]`, produced “No data to show” and zero marks despite its segment crossing the entire window. Scatter with the same x positions and zoom produced axes, no state message, and a reader summary saying there was no data. An all-invalid compact chart also suppressed its omission marker. The aligned check counts only sample centers, the scatter check counts points anywhere in the series, and the figure drops the note whenever the display is non-ready. Derive drawable content from the view’s draw ranges and visible points. Preserve F12/C5 disclosures when every value is omitted. [chart.ts:941](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:941) · [chart.ts:597](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:597)\n    24\t\n    25\t9. **M · Live-edge following survives a domain change that moves the window away from the edge. Ran.** I zoomed `[0,5,10]` to `[5,10]`, then replaced the data with a range ending at `15`. The displayed window remained `[5,10]`. Appending `20` jumped it to `[15,20]`. Plan 1.5 says a window away from the latest edge stays put. Reconcile the effective zoom and follow flag together whenever data or author bounds change. The existing follow test uses consecutive appends without an intervening domain update. [chart.ts:316](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:316) · [chart.ts:395](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:395)\n    26\t\n    27\t10. **M · Synchronous validation gives different answers depending on the entry point. Ran.** For a bar with `y.domain:[1,3]`, `validate()` returned `[]`, creation reported `AX110`, and a clean append removed `AX110` while the domain still excluded zero. Separately, a strict numeric chart threw `AX107` from `zoom(['oops','bad'])`, although spec 3.5 limits strict throws to create, update, and append. A rejected strict append also skipped console and listener delivery entirely. Share the DOM-free validation stages, retain the complete set of applicable findings separately from newly delivered findings, and make strict rejection specific to the public operation. Publish rejected-call diagnostics without replacing `chart.diagnostics`. [index.ts:41](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/index.ts:41) · [chart.ts:220](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:220) · [chart.ts:264](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:264)\n    28\t\n    29\t11. **M · Presentation diagnostics arrive late and outlive their cause. Ran.** A throwing tick formatter produced `AX160` with no reader note on the failing frame. Replacing it with a working formatter left `AX160` in `chart.diagnostics` and then displayed the stale warning note. A formatter that threw only for a hovered interior value added `AX160` to the getter without invoking `onDiagnostic` at discovery. The presentation map only inserts a code/field once, while disclosure is computed before formatting completes. Track findings by producing stage and revision, retire them when inputs change, and deliver pointer-origin findings immediately. [chart.ts:454](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:454) · [chart.ts:575](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:575) · [chart.ts:751](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:751)\n    30\t\n    31\t12. **M · Teardown leaves ownership behind in three lifecycle paths. Reasoned.** A retained destroyed handle still closes over `accepted`, the options store, source data, and DOM references. Removing a target without `destroy()` leaves document, media-query, and font listeners retaining the chart. A setup exception after the figure is appended but before the `try` around `update(input)` bypasses cleanup. Even ordinary teardown after drawing leaves chart-written `--axylo-backdrop` and series properties on the target. Use a disposable controller state, register cleanup as each setup step succeeds, restore owned styles, and release subscriptions on permanent detachment. The heap tests discard every handle. The pointer teardown test dispatches on the root, although the listener was attached to its child plot. [chart.ts:408](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:408) · [chart.ts:854](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:854) · [lifecycle.browser.test.ts:285](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/lifecycle.browser.test.ts:285)\n    32\t\n    33\t13. **M · A short, visible container can alternate between showing and hiding its fallback. Ran the controller transitions. Reasoned about CSS feedback.** Feeding plot heights `30,0,30,0` yielded summary visibility `true,false,true,false`. In a definite-height flex figure, showing the summary can consume the last 30 pixels, which hides the summary and gives those pixels back. Deferring the ResizeObserver callback moves this cycle across frames. Also, after a caption changes height, `size ??= measure()` can draw once at the previous size. Distinguish an externally hidden container from a visible figure whose caption consumed its plot space, and base L8 fallback on a stable available size. [chart.ts:602](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:602) · [chart.ts:612](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:612) · [css.ts:113](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:113)\n    34\t\n    35\t14. **M · Font loading invalidates layout but preserves fallback-font widths. Ran the measurer. Reasoned about browser typography.** A measuring context first returned `7` for a label, then `17` after a simulated font load. Even a new measurer for the same document returned the cached `7`. The width cache omits `fontEpoch`, and its 4,096-entry limit applies separately to an unbounded number of styles. A resize also leaves `textStyleDirty` untouched, so responsive CSS can change font or spacing without updating metrics. Invalidate measured widths on font load, bound the whole document cache, and reread computed typography on relevant size changes. Apply supported letter and word spacing to the measuring context as plan 2.2 specifies. [environment.ts:77](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/environment.ts:77) · [chart.ts:811](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:811) · [chart.ts:837](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:837)\n    36\t\n    37\t15. **M · Continuous bars get a second domain expansion that the layout cache cannot identify. Ran.** With an explicit x domain `[0,20]`, the chart emitted ticks from `-5` to `25`. With fixed bounds `[0,100]`, replacing two x positions `[10,20]` with `[10,90]` produced equal layout keys even though the requested projection changed from `[-5,105]` to `[-40,140]`. `barDomain()` adds spacing after the view has already selected the effective bounds. Use the view’s domain consistently for ticks, marks, and lookup. If layout needs a distinct projection, key its actual bounds. [axes.ts:76](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:76) · [axes.ts:123](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:123) · [axes.ts:143](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:143)\n    38\t\n    39\t16. **M · Donut color pins can paint the wrong slice. Ran the scene and theme inputs.** For `Empty:0, Sales:4` with a color pinned to `Sales`, the controller supplied palette keys `[\"Empty\",\"Sales\"]`. The sole visible arc requested palette index `0`, the `Empty` slot. This breaks DX6 precisely when two charts have different subsets of drawable slices. Build the theme binding array from each slice’s assigned `colorIndex` and author label. Test a zero-valued slice before a pinned positive slice. [chart.ts:469](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:469) · [view/donut.ts:61](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/view/donut.ts:61)\n    40\t\n    41\t17. **M · Static aligned charts eagerly copy borrowable columns, and domain-only updates pay that cost again. Ran.** For ascending `Float64Array` x and y columns, neither resulting frame buffer shared the caller’s buffer. All line, area, and bar creates go through the mutable streaming store. A change to `x.domain` alone then incremented the normalize counter. Plan 1.2 specifies borrowed typed columns, and 2.2 assigns author domains to the view stage. Preserve the borrowed frame until a write requires owned storage, and distinguish changes to parsing or fields from changes to presentation or bounds. [chart.ts:244](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:244) · [chart.ts:318](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:318) · [store-buffers.ts:26](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-buffers.ts:26)\n    42\t\n    43\t18. **M · Caption-only updates rebuild lookup, including the scatter spatial index. Ran the stage counters.** Updating only `description` reran `lookup`. Every `finish()` creates a fresh messages object, and lookup and reader both key on its identity. Separately, changing an aligned line’s interior sample count reran layout with the same endpoint ranges and tick inputs because the key includes slot indexes. Reuse resolved messages while overrides are unchanged, and include slot-dependent geometry only for chart types that consume it. The title-only test explicitly checks five unaffected stages and omits lookup. [chart.ts:273](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:273) · [chart.ts:649](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:649) · [lifecycle.browser.test.ts:173](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/lifecycle.browser.test.ts:173)\n    44\t\n    45\t19. **M · Figure naming and state text have inaccessible combinations. Reasoned from the figure. Ran the compact state model.** `labelledBy:'missing'` suppresses AX140 and installs a dangling ID reference without a fallback name. Providing both a valid `labelledBy` and a title still creates an internal heading, contrary to plan 2.4’s external-heading case. Generated IDs can also collide with an existing page ID such as `axylo-1-t`. On a compact loading chart with data, I observed the ordinary data summary as its description while “Loading chart” was only a descendant of `role=\"img\"`. Resolve the naming target, allocate collision-free IDs, and include the current state in the compact image’s accessible description. Test these combinations in the accessibility tree. [chart.ts:146](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:146) · [chart.ts:233](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:233) · [figure.ts:122](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:122)\n    46\t\n    47\t### Minor\n    48\t\n    49\t20. **m · The `validate()` type overload accepts options belonging to a different chart. Reasoned.** The first overload pairs any of `'line' | 'area' | 'bar'` with the union of all three option types. An area-only `stacked` or bar-only `layout` option can therefore type-check for `validate('line', …)` and then produce `AX150` at runtime. Give each discriminant its matching options overload. Add the negative example against the package entry point. The existing API examples import the separate declaration sketch. [index.ts:35](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/index.ts:35) · [examples.ts:2](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/api/examples.ts:2)\n    50\t\n    51\t### Verification\n    52\t\n    53\tNo files changed. No change to `contracts.ts` or `public.ts` is needed. `npm run typecheck` passed on the final run. I ran the three scoped core test files with Vitest’s filesystem caches disabled. The last lines were:\n    54\t\n    55\t```text\n    56\t Test Files  3 passed (3)\n    57\t      Tests  20 passed (20)\n    58\t   Start at  03:20:10\n    59\t   Duration  438ms (transform 68%, tests 16%, import 14%, worker 2%)\n    60\t```\n    61\t\n    62\tBrowser pixels, actual announcements, accessibility trees, heap behavior, and CSP enforcement remain unverified in this review. The scoped chart tests also lack end-to-end checks for continuous resize at the fallback boundary, late font metrics, compact 24×16 sizing, navigation through an intervening failed frame, and the reduced-motion first-frame comparison.\n    63\t\n    64\t### Areas examined and found sound\n    65\t\n    66\t- **Ordinary call order and coalescing.** Ran replacement → append → zoom and observed one draw with the requested window. Append → fresh data replacement discarded the append.\n    67\t- **Nested patch semantics.** Ran whole-object `title` and `x` replacements. Omitted nested properties reverted to defaults. The scoped property test also passed for absent and explicitly `undefined` keys.\n    68\t- **Ordinary explicit destruction.** Ran destroy before the first frame, repeated destroy, and subsequent update, append, and zoom. No later frame or stage ran.\n    69\t- **Console deduplication for accepted diagnostics.** The tests passed for one print per code per document and development-only hint printing. The weak document key and finite registry bound this cache.\n    70\t- **Environment resolution and DPR.** Ran locale override and document-language fallback. A simulated DPR change reran scene and draw while preserving normalization and layout.\n    71\t- **Text insertion and motion.** Source inspection found text-node insertion for author strings and formatter output, visually hidden summary text connected by `aria-describedby`, and no animation in the reviewed rendering path.\n    72\t- **Public loading and benchmark gating.** Both existing distribution bundles imported without a DOM and returned `AX103` for the invalid fixture. A production-mode controller exposed `__bench` only with the flag enabled. The renderer switch is absent from the public chart option types.\n     1\t**Four defects block release.** A paused chart can replay rejected or superseded data. A sliding category window can select a different datum from the one announced. Zoom can remove every way to reset the chart. A focused slider can retain a maximum that prevents assistive technology from reaching newly arrived data.\n     2\t\n     3\t**Ran** identifies results from the repository’s Node-compatible code. **Reasoned** identifies conclusions from tracing the DOM, controller, CSS, or tests. I did not launch a browser or screen reader.\n     4\t\n     5\t### Blocking\n     6\t\n     7\t1. **B · Paused appends violate call order and synchronous validation. Reasoned.** Pause a scatter chart, append A, replace the data with B, zoom, then resume. A is replayed against B using the later options and zoom. On a strict chart, an invalid paused append returns successfully. Resume catches the eventual exception, logs it, and discards the remaining queued batches, including valid ones. On aligned charts, even a *rejected* replacement can clear `held` before validation finishes. This extends the strict-rejection issue in the controller review to previously accepted buffered data. Apply each call transactionally to a pending state in call order, validate at the originating call, and freeze only the displayed revision. **I6, plan 1.5.** [chart.ts:257](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:257) · [chart.ts:358](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:358) · [chart.ts:475](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:475)\n     8\t\n     9\t2. **B · Category eviction changes the identity of keyboard focus. Ran the store and lookup. Reasoned through the slider and selection event.** With categories `A, B, C`, I focused B at ordinal 1 and appended D with `keep: 3`. The new frame contained `B, C, D` in the same epoch. Resolving the saved reference returned **C**, value 2, source row 2. Since the reference still compares equal, the focused slider can continue to say **B** while Enter selects **C**. Preserve the previous category key across a commit and remap it to the new frame before resolving focus, pins, or dismissal. Test both a surviving category and an evicted one. **A3, A7, `DatumRef`, plan 1.5.** [interaction.ts:960](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:960) · [focus.ts:31](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:31) · [store-buffers.ts:129](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-buffers.ts:129)\n    10\t\n    11\t3. **B · An empty zoom removes its own Reset control. Ran the view and zoom arithmetic. Reasoned through control removal.** On a numeric line with observations at `0,1,3,4,96,98,99,100`, one centered zoom produced `[25,75]` with zero value slots. The resulting empty state hides the proxy and removes Zoom out and Reset. Neither `0` nor a click can recover the original view. This makes the controller review’s empty-window finding worse. The same `ready` gate removes Resume from a paused stream that becomes empty, and suppresses the legend and table for an all-zero donut even though its model still contains the labels and zeros. Gate each control on the action it can perform. Keep recovery, Resume, and inspectable rows available in the relevant empty states. **I3, I6, F8, A2, A4, L7.** [chart.ts:605](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:605) · [interaction.ts:845](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:845) · [interaction.ts:869](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:869)\n    12\t\n    13\t4. **B · A focused slider freezes its native bounds as well as its text. Reasoned.** Focus a one-point chart, then append a second point. The reference and mode compare equal, so `writeProxy` returns before updating `max`, `value`, or `aria-valuetext`. A touch-reader increment encounters the old maximum of zero and can produce no `input` event. A physical arrow key happens to repair the bounds in `syncNative`. The same shortcut leaves an obsolete ordinal after eviction, an obsolete count after zoom, or old values, units, series names, and locale after an update. The AT-facing range needs to match each displayed revision. Diff its actual bounds, ordinal, and formatted text, keep unsolicited live announcements separate, and rehearse focused updates on the supported readers. **Decision 0001, A3, A7, WCAG 4.1.2, plan 1.5.** [interaction.ts:320](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:320) · [interaction.ts:337](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:337)\n    14\t\n    15\t### Major\n    16\t\n    17\t5. **M · `keep` does not bound retained memory. Ran the aligned store. Reasoned through controller ownership.** After 1,000 appends with `keep: 3`, the frame held 3 rows and the store reported **1,001 retained rows**. Retiring superseded revisions reduced retention to 3. The controller never calls `retire`. Paused scatter and donut charts additionally keep a copy of every incoming batch until Resume, even with `keep: 1`. Retain the displayed snapshot and the latest accepted state, retire superseded revisions, and apply retention to the pending store as data arrives. Preserve rows still addressable from the displayed frame. **I6, plan 1.5, P7.** [chart.ts:358](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:358) · [chart.ts:383](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:383) · [store.ts:453](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store.ts:453)\n    18\t\n    19\t6. **M · A clamped key can reverse the next assistive action. Reasoned.** Press Home at ordinal 0. The handler saves `intent = 'first'`, but the native value does not change, so no `input` clears it. An assistive increment to 1 then consumes the stale Home and returns to 0. Held keys at an endpoint have the same problem. A direct assistive value-set from 10 to 70 is interpreted as one page; a `change`-only notification has no handler. Also, tabbing onto a hovered plot sets `source = 'keyboard'` before `takeover` can adopt the pointer target. Scope key intent to its native action, reconcile the requested absolute ordinal once across supported event paths, and take over the pointer datum before changing source. **Decision 0001, A2, A3, WCAG 4.1.2.** [interaction.ts:432](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:432) · [interaction.ts:442](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:442) · [interaction.ts:458](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:458)\n    20\t\n    21\t7. **M · Keyboard exploration drops information available to the pointer. Ran.** With A at x=0 and 2 and hidden B at x=1, lookup counted three slots and the pointer reported “No observation” at 1. Right jumped directly from 0 to 2. For coincident scatter points, the pointer target contained two refs while the keyboard-created target contained one. On alternating scatter series, switching from A to B and pressing Right landed back on A. For a stacked area with values 2 and 3, the tooltip total was 5 and the all-series value text omitted it. On an incomplete stack, the text repeated “incomplete” per series and omitted the total. Use the lookup’s visible ordinal order and tooltip model for all-series navigation and text. Preserve the chosen series in narrowed mode. **Decision 0001, A2, A3, I1, §3.6.** [focus.ts:23](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:23) · [focus.ts:63](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:63) · [focus.ts:141](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:141) · [interaction.ts:381](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:381)\n    22\t\n    23\t8. **M · Panning and selection lack single-pointer equivalents. Reasoned.** Zoom in, then try to move the window right using taps or clicks alone. The toolbar only scales around the center or resets. Shift+Right, a drag, or a two-finger gesture can reach ranges that the buttons cannot. A mouse click and Enter/Space emit `select`; a touch tap only pins. A fresh mouse user also cannot explicitly select a secondary aligned series at the same x as the primary series. Provide single-click pan controls and a selectable datum or tooltip row that works with touch, mouse, and keyboard. **I3, I4, WCAG 2.5.1 and 2.5.7.** [interaction.ts:662](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:662) · [interaction.ts:691](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:691) · [interaction.ts:845](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:845)\n    24\t\n    25\t9. **M · Enabled zoom controls can do nothing or produce a zero-width window. Ran.** For `[0,100]` with two or three aligned x positions, the computed minimum width was 200 or 100. Zoom in returned `null` at full view. Drag accepts half that minimum, so one input method can reach a range another cannot. On scatter `[10¹⁶,10¹⁶+4]`, the second halving produced two identical endpoints. The focused wheel calls `preventDefault()` even when zoom cannot move. Category line, area, and bar all returned `false` from `zoomApplies`, although §3.6 gives the category exclusion specifically to bars. Use one representable minimum across gestures, enforce strictly ordered finite endpoints, disable exhausted controls, and consume the wheel only for an effective change. Implement ordinal zoom for supported category charts. **I3, I4, §3.6.** [focus.ts:282](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:282) · [focus.ts:298](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:298) · [interaction.ts:519](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:519) · [interaction.ts:656](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:656)\n    26\t\n    27\t10. **M · Gesture cancellation and pinch anchoring are inconsistent. Reasoned; ran the horizontal projection arithmetic.** Start a captured drag and press Escape. The document handler clears `down` without releasing capture or consuming the active cancellation, so a containing dialog can close too. There is no lost-capture or window-blur cleanup. A second non-touch pointer overwrites the drag, and a remaining pinch finger can be treated as a fresh tap after the other lifts. On a horizontal continuous bar axis, the pinch calculation measures the fraction downward while the scale increases upward. In a `[0,100]` projection, halving at the upper quarter moved the value under the fingers from 75 to 87.5. Give each gesture explicit pointer ownership, cancel and release it on every exit, suppress post-pinch taps, and derive the anchor fraction from the projection. **I3, I4, decision 0001.** [interaction.ts:609](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:609) · [interaction.ts:635](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:635) · [interaction.ts:737](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:737) · [interaction.ts:754](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:754)\n    28\t\n    29\t11. **M · A pinned scatter tooltip survives removal of its marks. Ran the lookup distinction. Reasoned through commit.** Tap to pin a scatter point, then programmatically zoom it out of view. Commit keeps the old target if `lookup.tooltip(oldTarget)` returns any rows. That lookup can format a source row outside the current view. I also obtained two tooltip rows for two previously coincident points after hiding both series in a new lookup. Validate pinned refs using their visible ordinals, rebuild the coincident set and count for the displayed revision, and dismiss when the pinned datum leaves it. **I1, A7, `PickTarget`, plan 1.5.** [interaction.ts:977](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:977) · [scatter.ts:159](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter.ts:159)\n    30\t\n    31\t12. **M · Tooltip positioning can cover a mark, escape the viewport, or be clipped. Reasoned.** Hover a chart under `transform: scale(2)`. Pointer deltas are viewport pixels passed to a layout-pixel lookup, and the tooltip translation mixes viewport bounds with unscaled `offsetWidth` and `offsetHeight`. In an overflow-clipped card, a candidate can fit the viewport but extend beyond the card. When no candidate fits, the last branch still shows a clamped rectangle, even across the active mark or when the tooltip is taller than the viewport. Scrolling a pinned or keyboard-focused chart does not recheck placement. Convert coordinates consistently, intersect clipping bounds, exclude the mark and focus ring, and use the readout when no candidate fits. **I1, A2, A6, WCAG 2.4.11.** [interaction.ts:296](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:296) · [interaction.ts:529](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:529) · [tooltip.ts:93](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:93)\n    32\t\n    33\t13. **M · The narrow readout covers the controls and disappears when approached. Reasoned.** In the 260 px tile, hover a point and move onto the readout. `pointerleave` exempts only the floating tooltip, so the readout disappears. When touch-pinned, the opaque readout sits directly over the toolbar at `z-index: 3`; tapping it counts as inside and cannot activate the button underneath. Keyboard dismissal also persists too long: dismiss at A, move to B, then return to A, and A is still suppressed. Reserve a reachable readout area, include it in hover persistence, and clear dismissal on the first target change from either input source. **I1, I4, WCAG 1.4.13 and 2.4.11.** [interaction.ts:534](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:534) · [interaction.ts:580](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:580) · [tooltip.ts:125](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:125) · [css.ts:142](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:142)\n    34\t\n    35\t14. **M · Keyboard focus can be entirely invisible on a donut. Ran the overlay and layout. Reasoned about clipping.** Tab to a donut whose first slice has value zero and whose second slice is positive. In a 320×200 layout, the plot occupied `(0,0,320,200)`. The first slice had no anchor and produced no overlay. The remaining CSS focus outline is drawn outside that exact rectangle and clipped by the plot’s `overflow: hidden`; the native input is transparent. Draw the plot ring inside its bounds and visibly identify the focused legend entry for an arcless slice. **F8, A2, WCAG 2.4.7.** [focus.ts:240](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:240) · [css.ts:128](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:128) · [css.ts:174](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:174)\n    36\t\n    37\t15. **M · Opening the table overflows fixed cards and moves auto-height neighbors. Reasoned.** Open a table in a short fixed-height card. The code freezes the plot at its former pixel height, then inserts the table and pager below the controls. A clipping card hides them; an unclipped card can cover the next chart. In an auto-height stack, following charts move. A 100 px plot can also receive a 160 px scroll region because of `Math.max(160, height)`. The 24-chart test compares fixed outer tile rectangles, which remain equal even when their contents overlap. Allocate a bounded, responsive table area and test actual content bounds after opening, resizing, and text zoom. **A4, A6, WCAG 1.4.4, 1.4.10 and 2.4.11.** [interaction.ts:786](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:786) · [interaction.ts:816](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:816) · [interaction.browser.test.ts:575](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/interaction.browser.test.ts:575)\n    38\t\n    39\t16. **M · An open table announces incoming data. Reasoned.** Leave page 1 open with 200 rows and append row 201. Rendering changes the polite region from “Page 1 of 2” to “Page 1 of 3” without reader action. Page clamping after eviction can do the same. The 24-stream test opens no tables and observes only live regions present at setup. Keep the visible count current and announce page changes only from reader-initiated paging or jumping. **A7, WCAG 4.1.3.** [table.ts:64](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/table.ts:64) · [table.ts:132](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/table.ts:132) · [interaction.browser.test.ts:467](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/interaction.browser.test.ts:467)\n    40\t\n    41\t17. **M · One `tabindex=\"0\"` does not guarantee that focus survives a render. Reasoned.** Focus legend B, then update wide fields from `[A,B]` to `[B,A]`. The renderer moves B using `insertBefore`; ordinary removal and reinsertion can drop focus. Its restoration path runs only when the key disappears. With focus in the jump field, disabling the table removes the active element without a handoff. Shrinking to one page likewise hides the focused pager. Preserve or restore the active control after reordering, and move focus to the disclosure, scroll region, or another surviving control before removing a focused subtree. **A2, A4, WCAG 2.4.3.** [toolbar.ts:94](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/toolbar.ts:94) · [toolbar.ts:135](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/toolbar.ts:135) · [interaction.ts:795](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:795) · [table.ts:123](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/table.ts:123)\n    42\t\n    43\t18. **M · “Jump to” can reject the displayed x or jump to another one. Ran the table model. Reasoned through the field.** The model accepted canonical ISO dates and instants, but rejected its own displayed `May 31, 2026` and `May 31, 2026, 12:00 AM UTC`. The field also rejects the displayed English `900,000`, while removing all whitespace turns `1 2` into 12. Its parser captures the x kind when the table opens, so changing a numeric axis to categories can coerce a valid category such as `002` into a different target. Invalid input only sets `aria-invalid`. Use the current model’s parser, preserve exact category labels, and provide an accepted-format example and visible, associated error text. **A4, A6, WCAG 3.3.1 and 3.3.2.** [interaction.ts:777](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:777) · [table.ts:144](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/table.ts:144)\n    44\t\n    45\t19. **M · The plot ignores translation keys and exposes English under the page language. Ran the value formatter. Reasoned through language inheritance.** Overrides for `pointAll`, `seriesValue`, and `position` still produced `0: a 2; b 3. Point 1 of 2.` The role description uses `typeLine` directly instead of `plotRole`. On a German page, the default slider label, role description, value text, generated summary, and polite state announcement can all inherit German. The note’s language also depends on *all three* note keys being untranslated, regardless of which sentence is displayed. Apply the existing message templates and assign language where each generated string is exposed. Give the range a label or description explaining navigation. **A3, A10, decision 0001.** [focus.ts:119](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:119) · [interaction.ts:942](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:942) · [chart.ts:756](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:756) · [figure.ts:182](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:182)\n    46\t\n    47\t20. **M · An axis can retain the wrong unit after an update. Ran.** I built a wide line with A and B both in `ms`, then changed only B to `s`. The production view and layout-input paths produced `Value (ms)` and `Value`, respectively, but `sameKey` returned `true`. The controller can therefore keep a milliseconds axis title while the tooltip and table use the new units. Include the effective axis title and shared unit in the layout key. **L6, plan 1.5.** [axes.ts:100](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:100) · [axes.ts:165](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:165)\n    48\t\n    49\t21. **M · The accessibility tests cannot establish several claimed outcomes. Reasoned from the tests.** `axNode` gets role, name, value, and maximum from Chrome, but gets its decisive spoken-text assertion directly from `getAttribute('aria-valuetext')`. The focus-obscuration assertion compares areas; a small tooltip can pass while completely covering the focused mark. The axe helper scans `body` with default rules and no explicit rule exclusions, but counts `incomplete` among rules that “ran.” The fixture loop covers four states and omits paused, zoomed, narrow-readout, and internal-error states. The pinch opt-out and donut overlay tests also omit the outcomes named in their titles. Assert computed AX output where available, report inconclusive rules separately, test actual intersections and state transitions, and record the five reader/browser rehearsals. I found no A9 conformance table with a test-existence check. **A2, A3, A6, A8, A9, I3.** [util.ts:97](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/util.ts:97) · [util.ts:118](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/util.ts:118) · [axe.browser.test.ts:62](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/axe.browser.test.ts:62) · [keyboard.browser.test.ts:214](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/keyboard.browser.test.ts:214)\n    50\t\n    51\t### Minor\n    52\t\n    53\t22. **m · High-contrast line swatches do not repeat the plotted dash. Reasoned.** Enable forced colors or increased contrast on a multi-line chart. The plotted lines switch to their contrast dash, while legend and tooltip swatches read only `cue.dash.normal`. Marker shapes still provide a cue, but the legend can show a solid sample for a dashed line. Bind swatches to the same normal and contrast patterns as the marks and inspect both at eight and more than eight series. **A5, F9, L2.** [swatch.ts:59](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/swatch.ts:59) · [css.ts:79](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:79)\n    54\t\n    55\t### Verification and interpretation\n    56\t\n    57\tI made no file changes. `npm run typecheck` passed. I ran the focus, axes, and reader suites in Vitest’s thread pool with filesystem caches disabled. The last lines were:\n    58\t\n    59\t```text\n    60\t Test Files  3 passed (3)\n    61\t      Tests  33 passed (33)\n    62\t   Start at  04:06:58\n    63\t   Duration  568ms (transform 48%, tests 40%, import 11%, worker 1%)\n    64\t```\n    65\t\n    66\tI treated §3.6’s “Yes” for line and area zoom as including categories. I3 explicitly mandates time, date, and numeric axes. I treated F8’s donut legend as an informational slice list and I2’s toggles as Cartesian series controls. The current checkout already provides the translation keys needed for finding 19. No change to `contracts.ts` or `public.ts` is required. Browser pixels, native event sequences across engines, actual announcements, and 400% reflow remain unverified.\n    67\t\n    68\t### Areas examined and found sound\n    69\t\n    70\t- **Ordinary zoom arithmetic — ran.** Halving around 0, 50, and 100 preserved the anchor, doubling returned to full view, and pan clamped at both edges. Ten thousand reciprocal wheel pairs drifted by about `1.4×10⁻¹⁴` on `[0,100]`. Calendar-date scaling preserved UTC positions.\n    71\t- **Ordinary wheel and page gestures — reasoned.** The wheel listener is explicitly non-passive. Unfocused, Ctrl-wheel, and Meta-wheel paths return before cancellation. Default touch handling allows page pan and pinch, and opt-in chart pinch retains one-finger page pan.\n    72\t- **Table semantics and laziness — ran the reader suite; inspected the DOM builder.** The aligned table addresses a distant page directly, renders at most 100 rows, retains hidden-series columns, and limits rows to the current x range. The DOM supplies a caption, scoped column and row headers, a named focusable scroll region, and guarded pager endpoints.\n    73\t- **Ordinary toolbar traversal and sizing — reasoned.** A populated stable toolbar has one tabbable button. Arrows wrap, Home/End reach the ends, Tab and Shift+Tab leave, and removing focused Reset hands focus to a surviving neighbor. Buttons specify a 24×24 CSS px minimum. Only the table headers are sticky.\n    74\t- **Hidden-series presentation — reasoned.** Legend toggles expose `aria-pressed`, retain the normal text color, and add a strike-through and hollow swatch. The table disclosure exposes `aria-expanded` and references the mounted table while open.\n    75\t- **Visible tooltip content — ran the lookup; inspected rendering.** “No observation” and “No data” remain distinct. The floating tooltip and readout share the same row renderer, overflow count, and stack-total rendering.\n    76\t- **Ordinary Escape and teardown — reasoned.** With the proxy focused, successive Escapes close the tooltip, leave single-series mode, then pass to the page. Explicit destruction removes the interaction layer’s document listeners and cancels its pending pinch frame.\n    77\t- **Compact interaction, motion, and the reader note — reasoned.** Compact charts omit the proxy and toolbar and install no plot interaction handlers. The reviewed styles introduce no animation. The full-chart note remains available as text with `aria-live=\"off\"`, independently of the polite state-change region.\n     1\t<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a1d73b9f46c46814f. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. -->\n     2\t\n     3\t## Report: chart core review fixes (Axylo)\n     4\t\n     5\tI followed AGENTS.md. I did not commit, and I did not touch contracts.ts, public.ts, globals.d.ts or any directory I don't own. All 20 findings are fixed and every test in my directories passes with both renderers. Two things are not done:\n     6\t- **Benchmark not run.** Another agent is changing `bench/` right now (details under \"Not done\").\n     7\t- **One finding was not reproduced in the browser:** finding 3 (see the table).\n     8\t\n     9\t### What I built\n    10\t**Core, rewritten into three files (`packages/axylo/src/core/`):**\n    11\t- **`controller.ts` (new):** the controller, with no DOM. Everything the page provides is passed in, so Node tests can drive it with a manual animation-frame queue and recording stand-ins (the reviewer's method).\n    12\t  - **Data path:** a chart that never appends uses `normalize` and keeps borrowed columns. The first `append` opens the store (`AlignedStore.fromFrame`, `PointStore` or `DonutStore`); the old row concatenation and `keep` counting are deleted.\n    13\t    - Every append is prepared, its view built and validated, then committed.\n    14\t    - Encoding changes after streaming re-encode the retained rows in a new epoch.\n    15\t    - `update({ data })` always replaces the stream.\n    16\t    - Older revisions are retired only after the next frame is drawn.\n    17\t    - Changes to a field's `domain`, `format` or `tickFormat`, or to `reference`, `zoom` or `colors`, never renormalize.\n    18\t  - **Diagnostics:** presentation diagnostics are kept per stage and per revision. Each finding is marked delivered before author code runs, and work stops if the chart was destroyed or changed meanwhile.\n    19\t  - **Failures:** an internal failure shows a complete error state and clears every cached output, so recovery redraws everything.\n    20\t  - **Sizing:** the too-small fallback is judged on the room a normal plot would get, and the figure is settled within the frame (for example the \"labels hidden\" note), so each mode is self-consistent.\n    21\t  - **Lifecycle:** a destroyed handle swaps its host for an inert one and drops its state.\n    22\t- **`chart.ts`:** the browser host.\n    23\t  - Each setup step registers its cleanup as it succeeds.\n    24\t  - Destroy removes the custom properties the chart wrote on the target.\n    25\t  - Generated ids are checked against the page so they can't collide.\n    26\t  - SVG is now the default renderer.\n    27\t  - When the target leaves the document, the resize observer notices and document-level watchers are released, then re-attached if it returns.\n    28\t- **`stages.ts` (new):** steps shared with `validate()`, so it returns the same view diagnostics as a created chart (AX110, AX130, AX131).\n    29\t- **`environment.ts`:** text measurement.\n    30\t  - The width cache is cleared on font load (`noteFontLoad`), with a per-document font epoch in the key.\n    31\t  - It is bounded for the whole document.\n    32\t  - Letter and word spacing are set on the measuring context.\n    33\t- **`axes.ts`:** the second x-domain expansion for bars is removed, and visible-slot indexes are no longer part of the layout key.\n    34\t- **`delivery.ts`:** a delivery pass now stops if the chart was destroyed or changed meanwhile.\n    35\t- **`focus.ts`:** the value text uses `pointAll`, `seriesValue` and `position`.\n    36\t\n    37\t**DOM (`packages/axylo/src/dom/`):**\n    38\t- `figure.ts`: new `top`, `side` and `body` slots, and `update` reports whether layout could have moved.\n    39\t- `interaction.ts`: `legend: 'top' | 'right' | 'bottom' | false`, `attach`/`detach` for document listeners, `plotRole` as the plot's role description, a Reset control in a zoomed empty window, and the open table freezes `body`.\n    40\t- Legend swatches (`swatch.ts`): filled square for bars and areas (with the bar pattern past eight series), line plus marker for lines, marker for scatter.\n    41\t- `tooltip.ts`: a labelled stack-total row using `total`.\n    42\t\n    43\t**Other files I own:**\n    44\t- `index.ts`: one `validate` overload per chart type.\n    45\t- `css.ts` (figure section only): `.axylo-body` and the top/side legend areas. Reference labels get a background plate in the backdrop colour via `box-shadow` 2 px. The text layer already exposes `data-role=\"reference\"`, so no change was needed there.\n    46\t\n    47\t**Tests:**\n    48\t- New: `test/core/controller.test.ts` and its host stand-in `host.ts`, `test/core/measure.test.ts`, `test/browser/chart/review.browser.test.ts` (26 tests).\n    49\t- `lifecycle.browser.test.ts`: a new test that a kept, destroyed handle releases its data and figure, and the pointer-teardown test now dispatches on the plot.\n    50\t- Running the suite on canvas: `AXYLO_RENDERER=canvas npm run test:browser` (handled in `test/browser/chart/util.ts`). Tests that give `__renderer` themselves keep their choice.\n    51\t- Expectations updated where the value text is now built from `pointAll`/`position`: no trailing period in all-series mode; role description \"Line chart\".\n    52\t\n    53\t**API examples:** `docs/api/examples.ts` now imports `packages/axylo/src/index`, with new `@ts-expect-error` cases (validate with mismatched options, `zoom`, `ordered`, `labelledBy`, `colors`, `compact`). `docs/api/tsconfig.json` was updated to match. **`docs/api/axylo.d.ts` can be deleted.**\n    54\t\n    55\t### Ran and saw\n    56\t- `npm run typecheck`: passes, including `docs/api` (so every `@ts-expect-error` fires).\n    57\t- `npx vitest run packages/axylo/test/core`: 8 files, 76 passed.\n    58\t- Owned browser directories (chart and a11y): 123/123 passed with SVG (the default), and 123/123 with canvas.\n    59\t- `npm run build`: OK.\n    60\t- `npm run test:browser` (whole suite): `Test Files 15 passed | 1 skipped (16)`, `Tests 237 passed | 1 skipped (238)`.\n    61\t- `npm test`: 620 passed, 7 failed, all outside my directories:\n    62\t  - `test/theme/palette.test.ts` (the palette is being changed; in an earlier run it was missing `research/palette/palette.json`).\n    63\t  - The data module's \"1M borrowed values under 100 ms\" timing test.\n    64\t  - In an earlier run, simplify's million-point timing test also failed while my browser tests were loading the machine.\n    65\t- **Pre-fix reproduction:** before rebuilding I ran `review.browser.test.ts` against the old bundle; 20 of the 21 tests there at the time failed. The retained-handle test also failed on the old bundle (10 references still alive).\n    66\t- **Gallery** (`light svg`, `dark canvas`): checked both images. Correct and readable, including the reference-label plate and the \"Values not shown: 3\" note; nothing to fix. Images are in `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-canarit--claude-spares-spare-6ClT4i/23402a37-81bb-469c-a14a-8bf7f048d066/scratchpad/core-fix/`.\n    67\t\n    68\t### Not done\n    69\t- **Benchmark not run.** Another agent is changing the harness: `bench/lib/driver.mjs` (04:49) and `build.mjs` (04:48) now expect slots, but `run.mjs` (03:22) still calls `startServer()` with no arguments. It fails with `TypeError … startServer (driver.mjs:22)`. I did rebuild bench's copy with `node bench/build.mjs`; the 6-block runs at 3×120 and 1×100,000 are still needed once the harness is consistent. Earlier SVG figures for comparison: 3×120 17.36 ms (the \"about 17.4\"), 1×100,000 78.82 ms [CI 64.54, 71.94 for the difference to uPlot].\n    70\t- **Bench adapter will change meaning.** `axylo-canvas` passes no `__renderer`, so with the new SVG default it would measure SVG. It must pass `__renderer: 'canvas'`.\n    71\t\n    72\t### Findings\n    73\t| # | Reproduced | Fixed | Covered by |\n    74\t|---|---|---|---|\n    75\t| 1 strict append | yes (browser, old bundle) | yes | controller.test \"finding 1\"; review \"strict ninth series\" |\n    76\t| 2 re-encode / replace | yes | yes | \"finding 2\"; review \"new y field…\" |\n    77\t| 3 hover after eviction | **no** (old bundle already had the store's retention) | yes (retire after the frame is drawn) | \"finding 3\"; review \"hover over the frame on screen\" |\n    78\t| 4 failure state | yes | yes | \"finding 4\"; review \"failures\" |\n    79\t| 5 controls / zoom and select events | yes (no select from a click) | yes, verified closed | \"finding 5\"; review \"Zoom in…\" |\n    80\t| 6 re-entrancy | yes (958 deliveries) | yes | \"finding 6\" (4 cases); review |\n    81\t| 7 scatter/donut append | yes | yes | \"finding 7\" (3, including paused); review |\n    82\t| 8 empty from draw ranges | yes | yes | \"finding 8\"; review |\n    83\t| 9 follow reconcile | yes | yes | \"finding 9\"; review |\n    84\t| 10 validate / strict parity | yes | yes | \"finding 10\"; review |\n    85\t| 11 presentation diagnostics | yes | yes | \"finding 11\"; review |\n    86\t| 12 teardown | yes (properties, detach, setup failure, kept handle) | yes | review \"lifecycle\"; lifecycle \"retains neither…\" |\n    87\t| 13 fallback stability | yes | yes | \"finding 13\" (Node model); review pixel stepping 120–229 px, both ways |\n    88\t| 14 fonts / measurement | Node only | yes | measure.test; \"finding 14\" |\n    89\t| 15 bar domain | yes (ticks −5…25) | yes | \"finding 15\"; review |\n    90\t| 16 donut pin | yes | yes | \"finding 16\"; review |\n    91\t| 17 borrowed columns | yes | yes | \"finding 17\" (buffer identity); review |\n    92\t| 18 stage counts | yes | yes | \"finding 18\" (every stage); review |\n    93\t| 19 naming | yes | yes | \"finding 19\"; review (3 tests) |\n    94\t| 20 validate overloads | type-level | yes | docs/api examples (`@ts-expect-error`) |\n    95\t\n    96\t### Choices I made where the brief was open\n    97\t- `legend: 'top' | 'right'` moves the whole toolbar, not just the legend entries, to keep one tab stop (A2). The table stays under the plot.\n    98\t- AX140 for an unresolved `labelledBy` is a presentation diagnostic, checked each frame. If a `title` exists, the title is used and AX140 is not raised.\n    99\t- A zoom window that can't be read is delivered to `onDiagnostic` and the console, then ignored; `chart.diagnostics` keeps the previous state.\n   100\t- A compact chart's description: state text only for loading and error; empty-state text plus the summary for empty.\n   101\t- On data replacement I normalize statically and drop the old store, rather than calling `prepareReplace`, so the borrowed path is kept.\n   102\t\n   103\t### Gaps in modules I compose\n   104\t- **view:** AX110, AX130 and AX131 are reported only when they are new against the previous view; the controller tracks the full set itself (`completeViewDiagnostics`).\n   105\t- **scene/bars.ts:** the bar pattern rule isn't exported, so I copied it in `interaction.ts`.\n   106\t- **render/text.ts:** nothing needed; `data-role` is already exposed.\n   107\t- **bench:** the `axylo-canvas` adapter issue above.\n   108\t- **tooltip placement (my `dom/tooltip.ts`, not fixed):** the tooltip can land under the pointer when the pointer sits between data points, so a click there selects nothing. Not among the findings; worth handing to the interaction reviewer.\n   109\t- **No contract changes needed.**\n   110\t\n     1\t<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a1d73b9f46c46814f, resumed. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. -->\n     2\t\n     3\t## Report: second fix pass (interaction and accessibility review, 22 findings) plus the later requests\n     4\t\n     5\tMost of it is done and tested against the real browser with both renderers. Two of my tests fail for reasons outside my files, and several items are only partly done (listed below). Nothing is committed, and I did not touch contracts.ts, public.ts, palette.ts, bench/ or the data module.\n     6\t\n     7\t### What I changed\n     8\t- **Interaction layer (`dom/interaction.ts`, rewritten):**\n     9\t  - Every listener on the chart's own elements is tied to one abort signal, so destroy removes them all.\n    10\t  - The plot's slider is compared with the frame on screen after each commit; its bounds, value and text are rewritten where they differ (finding 4).\n    11\t  - On a sliding category axis, focus, pin, dismissal and hover are moved to the same category's new place; a category that left the window moves to the next surviving one (finding 2).\n    12\t  - An empty zoomed window keeps the plot focusable with the `-`, `0` and Shift+arrow keys, plus Zoom out and Reset (finding 3). Each control is offered for what it can actually do; Resume, the table and the donut slice list stay available in empty states.\n    13\t  - Navigation keys go through the lookup rather than the browser's own range arithmetic; a direct value change from assistive technology (`input` or `change`) moves to that exact position (finding 6).\n    14\t  - Keyboard: scatter keeps the chosen series after a series switch, and coincident points show as one target (finding 7).\n    15\t  - Single-pointer paths (finding 8): a tap selects, a tooltip row can be clicked to select that series, and the zoom buttons zoom around the clicked or focused datum.\n    16\t  - Zoom limits (finding 9): one minimum window for every gesture, Zoom in marked unavailable when it can't narrow, and the wheel only consumed when it actually zooms.\n    17\t  - Gestures (finding 10): one pointer owns a drag; Escape cancels and consumes it; lost capture and window blur also end it; taps right after a pinch are ignored; pinch on horizontal bars now anchors correctly.\n    18\t  - A pinned tooltip is checked against the displayed frame and dropped when its datum leaves (finding 11).\n    19\t  - The narrow-tile readout can be reached and hovered; a touch-pinned readout lets taps through to the buttons under it (finding 13). A tooltip dismissed with Escape shows again after the keyboard moves away and back.\n    20\t  - Donut: the focused slice is marked in the slice list (also for a zero slice with no arc), and the focus ring is drawn inside the plot (finding 14).\n    21\t  - The open table now takes the plot's place at the plot's size, and the plot under it is inert (finding 15).\n    22\t  - Focus is restored after the legend reorders, and handed back to the chart when the table goes away (finding 17).\n    23\t  - \"Jump to\" accepts grouped numbers like \"200,000\" and dates as the table shows them (finding 18).\n    24\t  - Built-in English on the plot and in state announcements is marked `lang=\"en\"` on a foreign-language page (finding 19).\n    25\t- **Tooltip (`dom/tooltip.ts`):** stays clear of the active mark, the pointer and the focus ring. It stays inside every clipping ancestor. When no side fits, it uses the readout rather than covering the mark.\n    26\t- **Toolbar and table:** the toolbar marks unavailable buttons and gives focus back after a reorder. The table's page count stays silent while data arrives (finding 16).\n    27\t- **Swatches:** line swatches switch to the contrast dash where the lines do (finding 22). Area swatches now draw the series' marker on the chip (palette reviewer's A5 defect); bar chips are unchanged.\n    28\t- **`core/focus.ts`:** all-series value text uses what the tooltip shows, including the stack total once (finding 7). It also adds strictly ordered, finite zoom windows, the zoom-in availability check and stepping within one scatter series.\n    29\t- **`core/axes.ts`:** the layout cache key now includes the drawn axis titles, so a unit change redraws the title (finding 20).\n    30\t- **`core/controller.ts`:**\n    31\t  - While paused, the shown frame's rows are kept aside, so the store can drop everything older than its newest revision; `keep` now bounds a paused stream (finding 5).\n    32\t  - The note's language follows only the sentences it shows.\n    33\t  - The bench `describe()` now reports, for line charts, the row indexes the simplified drawing kept, plus the renderer kind.\n    34\t- **CSS (figure section):** table overlay, passive readout, focus ring drawn inside the plot, current legend slice, swatch dash switching, clickable tooltip rows.\n    35\t\n    36\t### Behaviour changes that required changing existing assertions\n    37\t- **Tab order with the table open:** now the table region (and its pager), then the toolbar; the covered plot is no longer a stop.\n    38\t- **Keyboard order:** an x that only a hidden series observes is now reachable and reads \"No observation\", as the lookup counts it. The old test said it was skipped; I reversed it, with the finding cited in the test.\n    39\t- **Donut \"Other\":** with ten slices, nine have a value, so seven are drawn and the rest are \"Other (2)\"; the zero slice H is listed on its own with no arc. I followed the view module's reading of F8 here; it is a reading, not something the spec states outright.\n    40\t- **Zoom out at full view:** shown but marked unavailable, so the toolbar doesn't reflow.\n    41\t\n    42\t### Ran and saw\n    43\t- **Typecheck:** passes.\n    44\t- **Node core tests:** 86 passed.\n    45\t- **Owned browser directories:**\n    46\t  - SVG: `Tests 2 failed | 157 passed (159)`.\n    47\t  - Canvas: `Tests 3 failed | 156 passed (159)`.\n    48\t- **`npm test`:** 1 failure, the data module's 1M-value timing test (not mine).\n    49\t- **`npm run test:browser`:** `Tests 2 failed | 267 passed | 1 skipped (270)`. That run came before the final changes (`zoomOut` gating, the hover, swatch and separator tests); the owned-directory runs above came after.\n    50\t\n    51\t**The failures:**\n    52\t- **Theme dark-toggle test (both renderers):** caused by the uncommitted palette edit. New LIGHT series 1 `#4395ea` and DARK `#1c73c5` differ by at most 39 per channel, inside the test's tolerance of 40, so the dark pixels count as light. It passed with the committed palette.\n    53\t- **New separator test, canvas only:** the seam between stacked bars falls across two half-tone rows (`100.168.237`, `251.230.212`), so no pixel is the background colour, which A5 requires. SVG draws a crisp seam. This needs pixel snapping in `render/canvas.ts` or `scene/bars.ts`, neither of which I own; I left the test failing.\n    54\t\n    55\t**Reproduction on 156f414:** I built 156f414 separately and ran the new browser tests against it.\n    56\t- 24 of the 30 tests in the second-pass file failed, each for the reviewer's reason.\n    57\t- The 6 that already passed: the three paused-chart tests (finding 1 was fixed by the first pass; Node tests also cover it), the Reset control, the accessibility-tree slider test, and the clipped card.\n    58\t- The benchmark agent's 10,000-point hover test also failed on 156f414 and passes now.\n    59\t\n    60\t### Benchmark agent's hover question\n    61\tReproduced on 156f414. The readout named only 1000, 3051, 5307 and 7563, matching the 4 distinct indices the agent saw.\n    62\t\n    63\t**Cause: the library, not the harness.** The old tooltip sat 12 px to the right of the active mark. Each rightward move of about 14 px landed on the tooltip, so the plot got `pointerleave` into the tooltip and kept the old datum until the pointer passed the tooltip.\n    64\t\n    65\t**Fixed:** the tooltip now keeps at least 22 px clear of the pointer. All 40 moves now read the nearest datum (within one index at this density), and all 40 are distinct.\n    66\t\n    67\t**Remaining limit:** a single move larger than the tooltip's clearance can still land on the hoverable tooltip, so a sweep of fewer, larger steps would stall again. Making the tooltip ignore the pointer entirely would conflict with WCAG 1.4.13 \"hoverable\"; that is your decision.\n    68\t\n    69\t### Findings\n    70\t| # | Reproduced on 156f414 | Fixed | Test |\n    71\t|---|---|---|---|\n    72\t| 1 paused order | no (first pass fixed it) | yes | review2 \"finding 1\" ×3; controller \"review 2, finding 1\" |\n    73\t| 2 category identity | yes | yes | review2 \"finding 2\" ×2 |\n    74\t| 3 empty-zoom recovery | yes | yes | review2 \"finding 3\" ×3 |\n    75\t| 4 stale range | yes | yes | review2 \"finding 4\" ×2, \"the plot as Chrome exposes it\" |\n    76\t| 5 keep retention | yes (Node, paused) | yes | controller \"review 2, finding 5\"; \"stores retire\" |\n    77\t| 6 stale key intent | yes | yes | review2 \"finding 6\" |\n    78\t| 7 keyboard vs pointer | not run on 156f414 | yes | focus2 \"finding 7\"; focus.test (reversed case) |\n    79\t| 8 single pointer | yes | partly: no pan buttons | review2 \"single-pointer\", \"selectable tooltip row\" |\n    80\t| 9 zoom limits | yes | yes, except category zoom | review2 \"finding 9\"; focus2 \"finding 9\" |\n    81\t| 10 gestures | yes (Escape) | yes; pinch arithmetic not tested | review2 \"finding 10\" |\n    82\t| 11 pinned survives | test written after the fix; not run on 156f414 | yes | review2 \"finding 11\" |\n    83\t| 12 placement | yes (pointer) | partly: not transforms or scroll | review2 tooltip ×2 |\n    84\t| 13 readout | yes | yes | review2 \"finding 13\" ×2 |\n    85\t| 14 donut focus | yes | yes | review2 \"finding 14\" |\n    86\t| 15 table overflow | yes | yes | review2 \"finding 15\"; keyboard (order) |\n    87\t| 16 table speaks | yes | yes | review2 \"finding 16\" |\n    88\t| 17 focus on render | yes ×2 | yes | review2 \"finding 17\" ×2 |\n    89\t| 18 jump to | yes | yes; visible error text needs a message key | review2 \"finding 18\" |\n    90\t| 19 language | yes | partly | review2 \"finding 19\" |\n    91\t| 20 unit key | not run on 156f414 | yes | focus2 \"finding 20\" |\n    92\t| 21 test strength | yes (by inspection) | partly | axe \"states the fixture loop does not reach\"; keyboard (intersection) |\n    93\t| 22 swatch dash | yes | yes | review2 \"finding 22\" |\n    94\t\n    95\t**Coordinator extras:**\n    96\t- Listeners removed on destroy: done (\"teardown\" test).\n    97\t- Click after hover reaches the plot: done (\"tooltip stays clear\" test).\n    98\t- Accessibility tree assertions: done where Chrome exposes the value. Chrome's tree still reports the number, not `aria-valuetext`, so value text is read from the attribute and the test says so.\n    99\t- Donut \"Other\" and donut legend tests strengthened from fixture values.\n   100\t- Area swatch markers: done.\n   101\t- Bar patterns in swatches: done.\n   102\t- Contrast dash compared with the plotted path: done (SVG only).\n   103\t- 1 px separator measured on pixels: done; fails on canvas, as above.\n   104\t\n   105\t### Not done or not observable\n   106\t- **Grayscale crossing-lines check (A5):** not done; telling three lines apart by marker in grayscale needs a person to look.\n   107\t- **Single-click pan buttons:** need message keys (`panLeft`/`panRight`). Until then, zoom around a clicked datum is the non-drag way to move the window.\n   108\t- **Ordinal zoom for category line and area:** needs a band scale with an offset in layout and scale. Category zoom stays off.\n   109\t- **Tooltip under CSS transforms and re-placement on scroll:** a scroll re-place was added but neither is tested.\n   110\t- **Visible \"Jump to\" error text:** needs a message key.\n   111\t- **Navigation instructions on the range:** need a message key.\n   112\t- **Summary language marking:** the generated summary mixes built-in text with series names, so it is not marked.\n   113\t- **Screen reader rehearsal and the A9 conformance table:** not done.\n   114\t- **Possible conflict with A7:** the focused range now rewrites its text when its position changes (for example \"Point 1 of 2\" after an append). Some screen readers may speak that; it needs rehearsal.\n   115\t\n   116\t### Contract changes needed\n   117\t- `Messages` (in `public.ts`) would need new keys: `panLeft`, `panRight`, a \"Jump to\" not-found/example text, and plot navigation instructions.\n   118\t- Nothing else.\n   119\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
