{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core2.review.md | sed -n '1,23p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core2.review.md | sed -n '1,23p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t**Four defects block release.** A paused chart can replay rejected or superseded data. A sliding category window can select a different datum from the one announced. Zoom can remove every way to reset the chart. A focused slider can retain a maximum that prevents assistive technology from reaching newly arrived data.\n     2\t\n     3\t**Ran** identifies results from the repository’s Node-compatible code. **Reasoned** identifies conclusions from tracing the DOM, controller, CSS, or tests. I did not launch a browser or screen reader.\n     4\t\n     5\t### Blocking\n     6\t\n     7\t1. **B · Paused appends violate call order and synchronous validation. Reasoned.** Pause a scatter chart, append A, replace the data with B, zoom, then resume. A is replayed against B using the later options and zoom. On a strict chart, an invalid paused append returns successfully. Resume catches the eventual exception, logs it, and discards the remaining queued batches, including valid ones. On aligned charts, even a *rejected* replacement can clear `held` before validation finishes. This extends the strict-rejection issue in the controller review to previously accepted buffered data. Apply each call transactionally to a pending state in call order, validate at the originating call, and freeze only the displayed revision. **I6, plan 1.5.** [chart.ts:257](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:257) · [chart.ts:358](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:358) · [chart.ts:475](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:475)\n     8\t\n     9\t2. **B · Category eviction changes the identity of keyboard focus. Ran the store and lookup. Reasoned through the slider and selection event.** With categories `A, B, C`, I focused B at ordinal 1 and appended D with `keep: 3`. The new frame contained `B, C, D` in the same epoch. Resolving the saved reference returned **C**, value 2, source row 2. Since the reference still compares equal, the focused slider can continue to say **B** while Enter selects **C**. Preserve the previous category key across a commit and remap it to the new frame before resolving focus, pins, or dismissal. Test both a surviving category and an evicted one. **A3, A7, `DatumRef`, plan 1.5.** [interaction.ts:960](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:960) · [focus.ts:31](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:31) · [store-buffers.ts:129](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-buffers.ts:129)\n    10\t\n    11\t3. **B · An empty zoom removes its own Reset control. Ran the view and zoom arithmetic. Reasoned through control removal.** On a numeric line with observations at `0,1,3,4,96,98,99,100`, one centered zoom produced `[25,75]` with zero value slots. The resulting empty state hides the proxy and removes Zoom out and Reset. Neither `0` nor a click can recover the original view. This makes the controller review’s empty-window finding worse. The same `ready` gate removes Resume from a paused stream that becomes empty, and suppresses the legend and table for an all-zero donut even though its model still contains the labels and zeros. Gate each control on the action it can perform. Keep recovery, Resume, and inspectable rows available in the relevant empty states. **I3, I6, F8, A2, A4, L7.** [chart.ts:605](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:605) · [interaction.ts:845](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:845) · [interaction.ts:869](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:869)\n    12\t\n    13\t4. **B · A focused slider freezes its native bounds as well as its text. Reasoned.** Focus a one-point chart, then append a second point. The reference and mode compare equal, so `writeProxy` returns before updating `max`, `value`, or `aria-valuetext`. A touch-reader increment encounters the old maximum of zero and can produce no `input` event. A physical arrow key happens to repair the bounds in `syncNative`. The same shortcut leaves an obsolete ordinal after eviction, an obsolete count after zoom, or old values, units, series names, and locale after an update. The AT-facing range needs to match each displayed revision. Diff its actual bounds, ordinal, and formatted text, keep unsolicited live announcements separate, and rehearse focused updates on the supported readers. **Decision 0001, A3, A7, WCAG 4.1.2, plan 1.5.** [interaction.ts:320](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:320) · [interaction.ts:337](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:337)\n    14\t\n    15\t### Major\n    16\t\n    17\t5. **M · `keep` does not bound retained memory. Ran the aligned store. Reasoned through controller ownership.** After 1,000 appends with `keep: 3`, the frame held 3 rows and the store reported **1,001 retained rows**. Retiring superseded revisions reduced retention to 3. The controller never calls `retire`. Paused scatter and donut charts additionally keep a copy of every incoming batch until Resume, even with `keep: 1`. Retain the displayed snapshot and the latest accepted state, retire superseded revisions, and apply retention to the pending store as data arrives. Preserve rows still addressable from the displayed frame. **I6, plan 1.5, P7.** [chart.ts:358](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:358) · [chart.ts:383](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:383) · [store.ts:453](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store.ts:453)\n    18\t\n    19\t6. **M · A clamped key can reverse the next assistive action. Reasoned.** Press Home at ordinal 0. The handler saves `intent = 'first'`, but the native value does not change, so no `input` clears it. An assistive increment to 1 then consumes the stale Home and returns to 0. Held keys at an endpoint have the same problem. A direct assistive value-set from 10 to 70 is interpreted as one page; a `change`-only notification has no handler. Also, tabbing onto a hovered plot sets `source = 'keyboard'` before `takeover` can adopt the pointer target. Scope key intent to its native action, reconcile the requested absolute ordinal once across supported event paths, and take over the pointer datum before changing source. **Decision 0001, A2, A3, WCAG 4.1.2.** [interaction.ts:432](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:432) · [interaction.ts:442](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:442) · [interaction.ts:458](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:458)\n    20\t\n    21\t7. **M · Keyboard exploration drops information available to the pointer. Ran.** With A at x=0 and 2 and hidden B at x=1, lookup counted three slots and the pointer reported “No observation” at 1. Right jumped directly from 0 to 2. For coincident scatter points, the pointer target contained two refs while the keyboard-created target contained one. On alternating scatter series, switching from A to B and pressing Right landed back on A. For a stacked area with values 2 and 3, the tooltip total was 5 and the all-series value text omitted it. On an incomplete stack, the text repeated “incomplete” per series and omitted the total. Use the lookup’s visible ordinal order and tooltip model for all-series navigation and text. Preserve the chosen series in narrowed mode. **Decision 0001, A2, A3, I1, §3.6.** [focus.ts:23](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:23) · [focus.ts:63](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:63) · [focus.ts:141](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:141) · [interaction.ts:381](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:381)\n    22\t\n    23\t8. **M · Panning and selection lack single-pointer equivalents. Reasoned.** Zoom in, then try to move the window right using taps or clicks alone. The toolbar only scales around the center or resets. Shift+Right, a drag, or a two-finger gesture can reach ranges that the buttons cannot. A mouse click and Enter/Space emit `select`; a touch tap only pins. A fresh mouse user also cannot explicitly select a secondary aligned series at the same x as the primary series. Provide single-click pan controls and a selectable datum or tooltip row that works with touch, mouse, and keyboard. **I3, I4, WCAG 2.5.1 and 2.5.7.** [interaction.ts:662](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:662) · [interaction.ts:691](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:691) · [interaction.ts:845](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:845)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
