{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core1.fix.report.md | sed -n '1,37p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a1d73b9f46c46814f. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. -->\n     2\t\n     3\t## Report: chart core review fixes (Axylo)\n     4\t\n     5\tI followed AGENTS.md. I did not commit, and I did not touch contracts.ts, public.ts, globals.d.ts or any directory I don't own. All 20 findings are fixed and every test in my directories passes with both renderers. Two things are not done:\n     6\t- **Benchmark not run.** Another agent is changing `bench/` right now (details under \"Not done\").\n     7\t- **One finding was not reproduced in the browser:** finding 3 (see the table).\n     8\t\n     9\t### What I built\n    10\t**Core, rewritten into three files (`packages/axylo/src/core/`):**\n    11\t- **`controller.ts` (new):** the controller, with no DOM. Everything the page provides is passed in, so Node tests can drive it with a manual animation-frame queue and recording stand-ins (the reviewer's method).\n    12\t  - **Data path:** a chart that never appends uses `normalize` and keeps borrowed columns. The first `append` opens the store (`AlignedStore.fromFrame`, `PointStore` or `DonutStore`); the old row concatenation and `keep` counting are deleted.\n    13\t    - Every append is prepared, its view built and validated, then committed.\n    14\t    - Encoding changes after streaming re-encode the retained rows in a new epoch.\n    15\t    - `update({ data })` always replaces the stream.\n    16\t    - Older revisions are retired only after the next frame is drawn.\n    17\t    - Changes to a field's `domain`, `format` or `tickFormat`, or to `reference`, `zoom` or `colors`, never renormalize.\n    18\t  - **Diagnostics:** presentation diagnostics are kept per stage and per revision. Each finding is marked delivered before author code runs, and work stops if the chart was destroyed or changed meanwhile.\n    19\t  - **Failures:** an internal failure shows a complete error state and clears every cached output, so recovery redraws everything.\n    20\t  - **Sizing:** the too-small fallback is judged on the room a normal plot would get, and the figure is settled within the frame (for example the \"labels hidden\" note), so each mode is self-consistent.\n    21\t  - **Lifecycle:** a destroyed handle swaps its host for an inert one and drops its state.\n    22\t- **`chart.ts`:** the browser host.\n    23\t  - Each setup step registers its cleanup as it succeeds.\n    24\t  - Destroy removes the custom properties the chart wrote on the target.\n    25\t  - Generated ids are checked against the page so they can't collide.\n    26\t  - SVG is now the default renderer.\n    27\t  - When the target leaves the document, the resize observer notices and document-level watchers are released, then re-attached if it returns.\n    28\t- **`stages.ts` (new):** steps shared with `validate()`, so it returns the same view diagnostics as a created chart (AX110, AX130, AX131).\n    29\t- **`environment.ts`:** text measurement.\n    30\t  - The width cache is cleared on font load (`noteFontLoad`), with a per-document font epoch in the key.\n    31\t  - It is bounded for the whole document.\n    32\t  - Letter and word spacing are set on the measuring context.\n    33\t- **`axes.ts`:** the second x-domain expansion for bars is removed, and visible-slot indexes are no longer part of the layout key.\n    34\t- **`delivery.ts`:** a delivery pass now stops if the chart was destroyed or changed meanwhile.\n    35\t- **`focus.ts`:** the value text uses `pointAll`, `seriesValue` and `position`.\n    36\t\n    37\t**DOM (`packages/axylo/src/dom/`):**\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'for f in packages/axylo/test/core/{measure.test,validate.test}.ts; do nl -ba \"$f\"; done\nrg -n \"(''^|'\"\\\\b)(it|test|describe)\\\\(\\\" packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/{review,lifecycle}.browser.test.ts\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'for f in packages/axylo/test/core/{measure.test,validate.test}.ts; do nl -ba \"$f\"; done\nrg -n \"(''^|'\"\\\\b)(it|test|describe)\\\\(\\\" packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/{review,lifecycle}.browser.test.ts\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t/**\n     2\t * Text measurement (plan 2.2, spec A6, L1): fonts that finish loading, a cache bound for the whole document,\n     3\t * and letter and word spacing applied to the measuring context. Finding 14 of the core review.\n     4\t */\n     5\timport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\n     6\timport { createMeasurer, measurementCacheSize, MEASUREMENT_CACHE_LIMIT, noteFontLoad } from '../../src/core/environment';\n     7\timport type { TextStyle } from '../../src/core/contracts';\n     8\t\n     9\t/** A document whose canvas context measures 7 px per character before a font loads and 17 px after. */\n    10\tfunction fakeDocument(options: { spacing: boolean }) {\n    11\t  const state = { loaded: false, set: [] as string[] };\n    12\t  const context: Record<string, unknown> = {\n    13\t    font: '10px sans-serif',\n    14\t    measureText(text: string) {\n    15\t      const letter = options.spacing ? parseFloat(String(context.letterSpacing)) : 0;\n    16\t      const word = options.spacing ? parseFloat(String(context.wordSpacing)) : 0;\n    17\t      const spaces = text.split(' ').length - 1;\n    18\t      return { width: text.length * (state.loaded ? 17 : 7) + letter * text.length + word * spaces };\n    19\t    },\n    20\t  };\n    21\t  if (options.spacing) {\n    22\t    let letterSpacing = '0px';\n    23\t    let wordSpacing = '0px';\n    24\t    Object.defineProperty(context, 'letterSpacing', { get: () => letterSpacing, set: (v: string) => { state.set.push(`letter ${v}`); letterSpacing = v; } });\n    25\t    Object.defineProperty(context, 'wordSpacing', { get: () => wordSpacing, set: (v: string) => { state.set.push(`word ${v}`); wordSpacing = v; } });\n    26\t  }\n    27\t  const doc = { createElement: () => ({ getContext: () => context }) } as unknown as Document;\n    28\t  return { doc, state };\n    29\t}\n    30\t\n    31\tconst style = (font = '400 12px Inter', letterSpacing = 0, wordSpacing = 0): TextStyle => ({ font, letterSpacing, wordSpacing, lineHeight: 15 });\n    32\t\n    33\tdescribe('text measurement (finding 14)', () => {\n    34\t  it('a font that finishes loading invalidates the widths measured with the fallback, for every measurer of the document', () => {\n    35\t    const { doc, state } = fakeDocument({ spacing: false });\n    36\t    const measurer = createMeasurer(doc);\n    37\t    expect(measurer.width('label', style())).toBe(35);\n    38\t    state.loaded = true;\n    39\t    // Until the load is noted, the cached width stands (the cache is what makes layout cheap).\n    40\t    expect(measurer.width('label', style())).toBe(35);\n    41\t    noteFontLoad(doc);\n    42\t    expect(measurer.width('label', style())).toBe(85);\n    43\t    expect(createMeasurer(doc).width('label', style())).toBe(85);\n    44\t  });\n    45\t\n    46\t  it('the cache is bounded for the whole document, across any number of styles', () => {\n    47\t    const { doc } = fakeDocument({ spacing: false });\n    48\t    const measurer = createMeasurer(doc);\n    49\t    for (let s = 0; s < 40; s++) for (let i = 0; i < 400; i++) measurer.width(`t${i}`, style(`400 ${10 + s}px Inter`));\n    50\t    expect(measurementCacheSize(doc)).toBeLessThanOrEqual(MEASUREMENT_CACHE_LIMIT);\n    51\t  });\n    52\t\n    53\t  it('letter and word spacing are set on a context that supports them, and added by hand otherwise', () => {\n    54\t    const spaced = fakeDocument({ spacing: true });\n    55\t    expect(createMeasurer(spaced.doc).width('a b', style('400 12px Inter', 2, 4))).toBe(3 * 7 + 2 * 3 + 4);\n    56\t    expect(spaced.state.set).toEqual(['letter 2px', 'word 4px']);\n  