{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"agent_message","text":"**Four defects block release at `4809516`.** A superseded frame can change the figure, Resume can remove the source rows of marks still on screen, a renderer exception can leave layers on different revisions, and a stream with `keep` can grow without bound when frames stop running.\n\n**Ran** means reproduced in Node with the manual frame host unless otherwise stated. **Reasoned** means traced through the source or tests.\n\n## Blocking\n\n1. **B · A superseded frame writes to the figure. Ran.** Draw data at x `[0,2]`, then update the title and data to `Intermediate` and `[5,7]`. Have a readout formatter call a second update for `[10,12]`. After one frame, the figure says `Intermediate` and the prepared controls use `[5,7]`, but the marks and committed lookup still use `[0,2]`. A formatter that calls `destroy()` also lets `figure.update()` run after host disposal. The lazy `reader.summary` runs author code inside the call to `figure.update()`, past the generation check. Plan §1.5 and DX5 require a single revision across the layers. Materialize formatter-dependent output before writing it, then check the generation before each host mutation that follows author code. [controller.ts](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:935)\n\n2. **B · Resume releases rows that the displayed lookup still needs. Ran on all five chart types.** Display a store-backed line window `[2,3]`, pause, and append `4` with `keep: 1`. Hovering `2` while paused returns its original row. Resume and hover again before the frame runs. The same mark and source index now return `row: null`. I also reproduced the loss when an append was pending at the time of Pause. The controller freezes `accepted.frame`, which can differ from the displayed frame, and discards the frozen rows in `accept()` before the replacement draws. This breaks plan §1.5, DX2 and DX5. Keep row ownership with the displayed snapshot until the replacement completes, including across Pause, Resume and re-encoding. [Freezing rows](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:550) · [Accepting the replacement](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:403)\n\n3. **B · An actual renderer exception can leave the marks, lookup and error message out of sync. Ran.** Draw `[0,2]`, then make the host text renderer throw and update to `[5,7]`. The new marks draw, the old interaction model remains, and the error message never appears. `showInternal()` retries the broken text renderer before clearing interaction or updating the figure. With a persistently throwing mark renderer, the error message appears over the old marks because clearing them calls the same renderer. Both recovered after restoring the host method and updating again. L7 and DX5 require a complete error revision. Disable interaction first, isolate each cleanup step, and let the host hide failed render surfaces independently of their draw methods. [Frame publication](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1055) · [Error fallback](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1117)\n\n4. **B · `keep` fails to bound a stream without successful frames. Ran.** Create a line with three rows and leave its first frame queued. After 1,000 one-row appends with `keep: 3`, the store reports **1,003 retained rows**. After 100 appends with `keep: 2` and a forced reader failure on every frame, it reports **102**. Retirement depends on the successful frame path. A zero-size flush has another problem. It commits new controls and retires the old source with the mark draw count unchanged. Plan §1.5 and P7 require bounded retention with correct provenance. Pin the displayed snapshot, release superseded pending revisions as calls arrive, and explicitly clear the display if an unmeasured or failed frame is going to release its source. [Draw and retirement](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1034) · [Failed frames](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1107)\n\n## Major\n\n5. **M · Re-encoding exposes paused arrivals, and a failed Resume loses the pending frame. Ran.** Pause a line displaying `[1,2,3]`, append `4` with `keep: 3`, then update `y` to another valid field. The chart shows `[2,3,4]` with Pause still active. In a second run, forcing the view stage to throw on Resume consumed the held frame. Removing the fault and making a valid title update recovered the chart without the buffered row. I6 and plan §1.5 require accepted arrivals to stay buffered until Resume. Re-encode the displayed and pending windows separately, and clear the pending frame only after its replacement is accepted. [Re-encoding](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:479) · [Resume](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:640)\n\n6. **M · Append validation writes to the wrong state. Ran.** A first strict append containing `NaN` throws AX103 but queues a frame and flips the chart’s streaming controls on. On a paused chart, adding series nine or donut slice nine leaves AX130 or AX121 out of `diagnostics` until Resume. `update({strict:true})` succeeds in between. In the other direction, a negative donut value buffered while paused adds AX120 immediately, then an unrelated resize applies that error to the previously healthy displayed ring. Plan §1.5, I6 and §3.5 require synchronous validation, rollback on strict rejection, and disclosure for the data being drawn. Set the streaming flag on acceptance and keep complete validation findings for the pending snapshot and display effects for the displayed snapshot. [Append transaction](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:523) · [Display state](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:721)\n\n7. **M · Re-entrant calls drop diagnostic and even