src/core/controller.ts:925)\n\n18. **M · An all-missing bar window suppresses the required missing marks. Ran.** Create bars `A: null` and `B: null`. The table contains both rows, but the controller shows “No data to show” and sends an empty scene. Its readiness check requires a finite value even though the bar scene can draw missing glyphs at the baseline. F2 requires those glyphs. Treat retained missing bar slots as drawable and reserve the empty state for a window with no drawable slots. [Display classification](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:721) · [Drawable-content check](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1368)\n\n19. **M · Environment changes can be missed or cause two draws in one frame. Ran the callback sequences. Reasoned through browser wiring.** After drawing at DPR 1, change the host to DPR 3 and signal reattachment. The committed ratio stays 1 until a separate DPR notification. Reattachment also leaves the font epoch alone, so a font load missed while detached can leave cached widths in use. Changing only the document’s `lang` has no watcher. Conversely, executing the scheduled data update and then the theme watcher’s callback produces two draws in the same frame callback batch. Plan §2.2, F5, F6 and the renderer contract require fresh environment inputs and one mark draw per animation frame. Refresh inputs on reattachment, watch language changes, and feed theme invalidation into the same frame scheduler. [Controller invalidation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1211) · [Reattachment](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:109) · [Theme watcher](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/watch.ts:11)\n\n20. **m · Several regression tests can pass when the behavior named in the test is broken. Reasoned from assertions. Ran the host accessor check.** The Node re-entrancy test receives AX140 before its `chart` variable i